    id: 'r2-03', level: 'standard', genre: 'dialogue', title: 'Welcoming Students from Australia',
    text: `Ms. Green: Next month, ten students from our sister school in Australia will visit us for a week. I'd like you to think about how to welcome them.\nKen: That sounds exciting! How about a welcome party in the gym? We can play Japanese songs and eat sushi together.\nYui: That's a nice idea, but some of them may not eat raw fish. Ms. Green, what do you think?\nMs. Green: Good point, Yui. In Australia, many people eat fish, but raw fish isn't so common. Also, one of the students doesn't eat meat. So it is better to prepare several kinds of food.\nKen: I see. Then how about making onigiri? We can put different things inside, like salmon, ume, and kombu. They can choose ①<u>the ones</u> they like.\nYui: Great! We can also make them together with the students. Cooking together is a good way to become friends.\nMs. Green: I love that idea. What else do you want to do?\nYui: I want to show them our town. There is an old shrine near our school, and its autumn festival will be held during their stay.\nKen: But they don't know anything about the festival. ②<u>If they just watch it, they may not enjoy it so much.</u>\nYui: You're right. Then we can make a short guidebook in English about the history of the festival before they come.\nMs. Green: Wonderful. I think they will be glad to understand what they are seeing. By the way, I have one more piece of advice. In Australia, students usually say what they think in class, even when the teacher doesn't ask them. So please don't be surprised if they talk a lot in your lessons.\nKen: Really? In Japan, most students wait until the teacher asks them a question.\nYui: That's interesting. I think we can learn a lot from each other. Maybe we should also tell them about Japanese school life, like cleaning our classrooms.\nMs. Green: Yes. When they come here, don't just teach them about Japan. Ask them about Australia, too. Learning about different cultures is not a one-way street.\nKen: OK. Let's ask them to bring photos of their school and town!\nYui: I can't wait to meet them.`,
