    id: 'r2-04', level: 'standard', genre: 'email', title: 'Emails before a Homestay',
    text: `Dear Mrs. Wilson,\nHello. My name is Haruka Mori. I'm a fifteen-year-old student from Japan. I'm going to stay with your family for two weeks this summer. Thank you very much for accepting me.\nLet me tell you a little about myself. I live in a small city in Nagano with my parents and my little brother. I'm a member of the art club at school, and I like drawing pictures of mountains and animals. I heard that there are beautiful lakes near your house. I'd like to draw them.\nI have some questions. First, what kind of clothes should I bring? It gets very hot in Nagano in August, so I only have summer clothes. Second, I want to bring a present for your family. What do you like? Finally, I'm worried about my English. I can read it well, but speaking is difficult for me. Will people understand me?\nI'm looking forward to meeting you.\nBest wishes,\nHaruka\n\nDear Haruka,\nThank you for your email. We are all very happy that you are coming! There are three people in our family: my husband Tom, our son Leo, who is twelve, and me. We also have a dog named Max.\nHere are the answers to your questions. ①<u>About clothes, please bring a jacket.</u> Summer days are warm here, but it can be cold in the morning and at night, especially near the lakes. We often go camping, so good shoes are also important.\nAbout a present, please don't worry too much. Anything small is fine. Leo loves Japanese anime, so he would be glad to get something about it. But to be honest, I would be happiest if you drew a picture of our family. We would put it on the wall in the living room.\nAbout English, don't be afraid of making mistakes. Everyone makes mistakes when they learn a new language. Leo is learning French at school, and he makes a lot of mistakes, too. The important thing is to try. If you don't understand something, just say, "Could you say that again?" We will speak slowly for you.\nWe will meet you at the airport on August 3. See you soon!\nLove,\nLinda Wilson`,
